  "notes": "Single CSS property with four keyword values — one overview page documents the full surface; no member is substantial enough to need a child route. The property definition table and value prose are quoted from the css-text-decor-4 ED fetched 2026-10-18. Two honest ambiguities are preserved rather than resolved: (1) the draft's inline editor's issue questions whether the initial value should be none for web compatibility (issue #4653), so the page warns against depending on default-state rendering; (2) the trunk runtime flag reads experimental while the milestone listing, BCD, and webstatus.dev all record Chrome 155 shipped — both facts are disclosed side by side with feature-detection guidance. Lifecycle for a CSS property = cascade/inheritance/animation behavior, documented via the propdef rows (inherited: yes; computed value; discrete animation).",
